<p>I walk to the altar. The stone is cold under my bare feet. I lie down. The surface is hard — unyielding, the way stone is, the way the world is. My back presses against it. My shoulders. My buttocks. My heels. Every point of contact is a cold, factual reminder that I am here, I am real, this is happening.</p>

